{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352150758,"sessionID":"ses_e3855e53fffeIUEfdSrshjh8xm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7b8f8c60010h97TRBFgua5Cq","messageID":"msg_1c7b8b9440017UYtktBQLzA2es","sessionID":"ses_e3855e53fffeIUEfdSrshjh8xm","type":"text","text":"All verified. Final state:\n\n- **Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask + stdlib `sqlite3`, DB at `./data/inventory.db`. Token auth (`Bearer`), register/login/logout, paged item list with `q`/`location`/`low_stock` filters, CRUD (PUT keeps quantity, duplicate SKU → 409), movements with over-draw refused (400) and `low_stock = quantity <= reorder_level`. Anyone reads; writes need a token.\n- **Deps**: `backend/requirements.txt` now fully pinned+hashed so the Dockerfile's hash-mode install succeeds (previously it failed; verified in a clean venv).\n- **Frontend**: React+TS+Vite with Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`); auth screen, inventory table with highlighted low-stock rows, debounced search, location filter, low-stock switch, paging, item page with receive/take-out forms updating the quantity, add/edit forms surfacing API errors (incl. duplicate SKU), delete with `window.confirm`; hash routing served by the SPA fallback.\n- **Tested end-to-end on gunicorn:8000**: health, auth, all endpoints, restart persistence, traversal-safe static serving, `tsc` clean, production build OK.","time":{"start":1794352150726,"end":1794352150730}}}
